# Architecture

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/00-overview/current-state.md` before significant work.

- Modular monolith: one Laravel app, one Inertia/React frontend, one PostgreSQL, one Redis. No microservices.
- Domain logic lives in `app/Domain/<Domain>/` (Actions, Models, Events, Policies, Services). Controllers stay thin.
- **Configure, don't hard-code.** One reusable module/engine, configured per business type and tenant.

```php
// ❌ BAD
class SalonLeadService {}
if ($tenant->business_type === 'salon') { /* salon-only branch */ }

// ✅ GOOD
class LeadService {}                               // one Lead module
$tenant->modules()->enabled('booking');            // behaviour driven by config
```

- Customization order: Configuration → Custom Field → Workflow → Reusable Module → Engine Enhancement → Tenant Extension.
- Every tenant-owned query is scoped by the server-side `TenantContext`. Never trust a client `tenant_id`.
- Vendors (AI, messaging, payments) are behind interfaces; business code never calls vendor SDKs directly.
- AI never decides price, stock, availability, booking/payment/order status.
- Architectural change ⇒ write/update an ADR in `docs/12-decisions/` first.
- No unrelated refactors, renames or dependency upgrades inside a feature task.
- Do not implement roadmap items that were not requested. Prefer simple, reusable, testable.
